+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2KC7W3QM0V86PVA3SVA01FN","recordedAt":"2026-09-15T23:48:58Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"db-models/onfinance-db-model-master: Cleartext broker credentials modelled in the secrets MongoDB collection","description":"onfinance_db_model_master/models.py:8-15 (Secrets Document) declares apiKey, zerodha_username, zerodha_password, zerodha_2fa, apiSecrets, accessToken and accountName as plain StringField, so any service that persists this model stores Zerodha broker login credentials, the TOTP 2FA seed, API secrets and access tokens unencrypted in the db-models-mongodb.default.secrets MongoDB collection. company-profile/example-co/sdlc/metastore.json classifies zerodha_password, zerodha_2fa, apiSecrets and accessToken as restricted and spdi personal data, and policy.json requires secrets in aws-secrets-manager (90-day rotation), which this model bypasses by design. The same root cause covers the user collection: user_password BinaryField (models.py:390) and user_binance_auth_creds DynamicField (models.py:397); one fix covers both locations. Reviewed at commit 70b3633e171a1b8d389b27bb901c84c34a0e9bf6; SARIF result ruleId asvs-v14-sensitive-storage (fail). SLA topic: encryption.\n\nData flow: Secrets Document fields (apiKey, zerodha_password, zerodha_2fa, apiSecrets, accessToken as StringField, models.py:8-15) -> mongoengine Document persistence -> db-models-mongodb.default.secrets collection stored in cleartext; same pattern user_password models.py:390 and user_binance_auth_creds models.py:397 -> user collection\n\nExploit scenario: An attacker with read access to the db-models-mongodb instance (dev database, or a consuming-service backup, export or staging copy of these collections) reads zerodha_password, zerodha_2fa and accessToken values verbatim with no decryption or cracking, then authenticates to the linked brokerage account as the record owner by replaying the password plus the 2FA seed and calls the broker API with the plaintext accessToken.\n\nImpact: Disclosure of restricted SPDI credentials for every record persisted through this model: broker password, 2FA seed, API secret and access token exposure is direct account takeover of the linked brokerage account, not just data disclosure, and a reportable personal-data breach for this SEBI broker and RBI NBFC. Context that does not lower severity: db-models runs in the dev tier with isolated exposure and no network entry points of its own, and the catalog severity high of sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S1 stands for an unencrypted store carrying regulatory data regardless of tier.\n\nRemediation: Move credential values to the policy secrets backend (aws-secrets-manager per company-profile/example-co/sdlc/policy.json secretsManagement.backend) and keep only a locator reference in the document; where database residency is required, wrap the fields in application-level envelope encryption (AES-256-GCM keyed from KMS) and mask on serialisation; store user_password only as an irreversible hash (bcrypt or argon2) instead of a raw BinaryField; add a model test asserting no credential field round-trips unencrypted.\n\nSource: maxwell-secure-code-reviewer agent analysis (execute-scr) at pinned commit 70b3633e171a1b8d389b27bb901c84c34a0e9bf6; no scanner SARIF log exists for this target (scanners could not run: no scanner executor configured).","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S1","sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S4","dpdp-rules-2025:6(1)(a)"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.DS.S1"},{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.DS.S4"},{"regulator":"MeitY","instrument":"dpdp-rules-2025","controlId":"6(1)(a)"},{"regulator":"ISO","instrument":"iso-27001-2022","controlId":"A.8.24"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"db-models","repoId":"onfinance-db-model-master"},"location":{"path":"onfinance_db_model_master/models.py","startLine":8,"endLine":15},"fingerprint":"28400f1691cdcc54398af1aa8f2b4dcc04972c4447af17da5593aa45e3c99a12","source":{"kind":"agent-analysis","ruleId":"asvs-v14-sensitive-storage","tool":"secure-code-reviewer"},"status":"triaged","slaDueAt":"2026-09-22T19:42:44Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.MA.S3","topic":"patch-sla","severity":"high","days":7},"relatedObservationIds":["obs_01M2KC7W3PZKM33CSP1PACFA2F"],"firstSeenAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/db-models/repos/onfinance-db-model-master/onfinance_db_model_master/models.py","sha256":"7f6eb5d6f2beb71e698ada8a80adaee08fb316afe8d9ed3c25238e33ba46b553","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","description":"lines 8-15, 390, 397 at 70b3633: Secrets credential fields, user_password, user_binance_auth_creds"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"company-profile/example-co/sdlc/metastore.json","sha256":"36ad5b400be470c4363b0c7d043dc871e8c7cc1a4a8c0ddbaec21891b83191ef","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","description":"secrets and user collections classified restricted/spdi in db-models-mongodb.default"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"company-profile/example-co/sdlc/policy.json","sha256":"e92e455ff786a63021d80925ebeb905f4b8cf16ba106ac77ed361322ef627d06","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","description":"secretsManagement.backend aws-secrets-manager, rotationDays 90"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/db-models/env/dev.json","sha256":"04551256d13e65a22a744116d0246d28c3e0398150673f96765a46b4696debe1","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","description":"tier dev, exposure isolated, dataClassification internal"},{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/opencode/453ecc6e-1346-418f-a2c0-1bfcead851c3.execute-scr.db-models.onfinance-db-model-master.sarif.export.json","sha256":"34cdbb5601170c9c81efd702b13f8a36f28b684ed8fad2357266389e81454831","collectedAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","description":"fail result asvs-v14-sensitive-