+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2K7B0MJJVWFWXF6KZ783GFZ","recordedAt":"2026-09-15T23:48:58Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"connect and switch-connection accept model-controlled connection strings with no host allow-list","description":"src/tools/mongodb/connect/connect.ts:14: `connectionString: z.string().describe(\"MongoDB connection string (in the mongodb:// or mongodb+srv:// format)\")` (and switchConnection.ts:13-20). The value is passed to session.connectToMongoDB and on to the driver with no host allow-list or scheme enforcement (src/common/session.ts:148, src/common/connectionManager.ts). A hijacked or prompt-injected agent can redirect the session - and every subsequent find, aggregate, export or insert call - to an attacker-chosen host, exfiltrating client data from the gateway network position or pointing the gateway at an unapproved cluster; connect-type tools also stay enabled in readOnly mode. No egress class (offline, loopback-only, governed) is declared or enforced anywhere in the server, against the reference harness architecture requirement. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S2. SLA topic: patch-sla. Refutation: evidence lens not refuted (Every material claim verified in files I opened: connect.ts:14 declares connectionString: z.string() with no allow-list and passes it via session.connectToMongoDB (session.ts:148-150) and MCPConnectionManager.connect (connectionManager.ts:286-342, no host or scheme validation), switchConnection.ts:13-20 matches verbatim, readOnly mode explicitly allows operationType 'connect' (tool.ts:761) with disabledTools defaulting to [] (userConfig.ts:74-78), no egress-class/allow-list/NetworkPolicy compensating control exists anywhere in the repo or deploy/, the repo is deployed in dev/qa/prod (prod exposure partner) at the pinned commit aaa72a0, severity high equals both the sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S2 catalog defaultSeverity and the SARIF rule's own defaultSeverity, and the cited SARIF export contains an AGENT-ASI03-03 result (ruleIndex 5) at src/tools/mongodb/connect/connect.ts region 13-17 carrying the candidate's exact fingerprint and the candidate's four regulatoryRefs; two non-blocking notes: evidence[1] is a bare duplicate of evidence[0] (same ref and sha256, no description), and the 'result 6' ordinal in evidence[0].description is consistent with the rule's 1-based position (ruleIndex 5) but the results[] array index could not be independently counted.); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (Not refuted: sebi-cscrf-2024 binds example-co (stock-broker/depository-participant entityTypes, active mid-size-re SEBI registrations, IN, in frameworksInScope) and is cited first; both controlIds exist in its catalog and cover the described gap (PR.AA.S2 'Protect network integrity through segregation and segmentation' requires whitelist-based configuration of IPs/ports/services with ACLs and evidence of whitelist-based inbound and outbound control; PR.DS.S4 'Prevent data leaks' expects egress DLP/allow-listing on data exports), and both carry defaultSeverity high, which is exactly the candidate's severity basis and the correct maxwell-conventions section 4 derivation since the candidate has no CVSS score and the auditor's emission spec gives its SARIF rules only properties.defaultSeverity, no security-severity; the OWASP Agentic ref ASI03 (identity/privilege abuse - model wields the gateway's unscoped network egress and model-chosen connection credentials) matches its single owasp-agentic-top10-2026:asi03 tag and the pre-declared AGENT-ASI03-03 rule row in .claude/agents/agent-graph-auditor.md ('no egress class declared or enforced... no domain allow-list' - sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S2, sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S4, ASI03, csa-mcp-security-2025:8.3) which the candidate follows verbatim, and owasp-agentic-top10-2026 and csa-mcp-security-2025 are in the vocab as cross-sector voluntary instruments properly cited as secondary refs (skill section 1 typical selections for a company running LLM agents); the patch-sla topic named in the description is a valid sla-table topic for this fixable misconfiguration (SEBI patch-sla rows exist) and slaBasis/slaDueAt are the ledger keeper's; the one thing I could not open is the SARIF export's content beyond its first 2000 characters (single minified line defeats both Read and Grep - control strings visible in the read head return no grep matches), which does not change the mapping because the rule crosswalk is declared in the auditor file and severity resolves through the catalog regardless, and the candidate's evidence sha256 matches the workflow-provided sarifSha256 exactly.).","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S2","sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S4"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.AA.S2"},{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.DS.S4"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-agentic-top10-2026","controlId":"ASI03"},{"regulator":"CSA","instrument":"csa-mcp-security-2025","controlId":"8.3"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":"src/tools/mongodb/connect/connect.ts","startLine":13,"endLine":17},"fingerprint":"459db0ab83c6b05556a5b5f35c1ffff1a3440895d64fbd3e73c3501430f06ba1","source":{"kind":"sarif","ruleId":"AGENT-ASI03-03","tool":"maxwell-agent-graph-auditor","toolVersion":"1.0.0"},"status":"triaged","slaDueAt":"2026-09-22T15:14:31Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.MA.S3","topic":"patch-sla","severity":"high","days":7},"relatedObservationIds":["obs_01M2K7B0MGN03WM0T8X8C9WZTT","obs_01M2K7B0MGNJTVJWN1NR4KP3F2"],"firstSeenAt":"2026-09-15T15:14:31Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-15T15:14:31Z","evidence":[{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/opencode/run_01M2GDZ3Q3S5WYCB3MV02QJXZ1.probe-agent-graph.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","sha256":"c3c7b9dc736d1407d