+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2K7B0MJ68AR00YTNE2N00V2","recordedAt":"2026-09-15T23:48:58Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"MongoDB MCP confirmation gate fails open: destructive tools execute without human approval","description":"src/elicitation.ts:31-33: `if (!this.supportsElicitation()) { return true; }` - Elicitation.requestConfirmation returns true whenever the connected MCP client does not advertise elicitation capability, so the eight destructive tools gated by the default confirmationRequiredTools (drop-database, drop-collection, delete-many, drop-index, atlas-create-access-list, atlas-create-db-user, atlas-streams-manage, atlas-streams-teardown) execute with no human confirmation against elicitation-incapable clients, which includes common headless agent harnesses. ToolBase.verifyConfirmed (src/tools/tool.ts:609-615) delegates the entire approval gate to this method, and the default config (userConfig.ts:79-94) defines no other approval path. This is the deployed agent gateway for app mcp-gateway (qa and prod, EKS ap-south-1, partner exposure, data classes pii and financial, supports the order-routing critical function) and sdlc/policy.json aiCodingPolicy.humanReviewRequired is true. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S3. SLA topic: patch-sla. Refutation: evidence lens not refuted (Every material claim verifies in files I opened: src/elicitation.ts:31-33 returns true whenever the client cannot elicit, src/tools/tool.ts:491-515 and 609-615 show this is the only approval gate for the exactly-eight default confirmationRequiredTools listed at src/common/config/userConfig.ts:79-94, no deployed override compensates (deploy/aws/Dockerfile - the qa/prod IaC root per env/qa.json, env/prod.json - disables only atlas-local and sets no MDB_MCP_READ_ONLY, and the azure bicep's readOnly default is overridden to \"false\" in both parameter templates), qa and prod exist on EKS ap-south-1 with pii/financial data classes (prod partner-exposed; qa is internal, a harmless compression in the description's parenthetical), details.json maps the order-routing critical function to mcp-gateway, sdlc/policy.json has aiCodingPolicy.humanReviewRequired true, the checkout .git/HEAD equals the pinned commit aaa72a040db4c32f3d6488d5e28e2892a68e9ee0, the SARIF export exists and contains the AGENT-ASI09-01 rule and a result with ruleId AGENT-ASI09-01 at src/elicitation.ts startLine 30 carrying the identical fingerprint f658ce80...cb0f0, and severity high equals both the SARIF rule's and the sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S3 catalog defaultSeverity (line 2249); evidence[1] is a bare duplicate of evidence[0] but both entries resolve and support the claim, so it is redundant rather than refuting.); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (All three cited instruments apply to example-co and are correctly ordered - sebi-cscrf-2024 (active mid-size-re stock-broker/DP, in frameworksInScope) first with PR.AA.S3 (catalog prose 'Least Privilege ... along with segregation of duties', the auditor's prescribed mapping for AGENT-ASI09-01, defaultSeverity high matching the candidate's severity since no CVSS or SARIF security-severity score exists on the candidate or the rule, and the rule's error level would also map high so the generic-lens vs skill ordering discrepancy is immaterial), then owasp-agentic-top10-2026 ASI09 (trust exploitation, matching the single asi09 tag and the fails-open human-approval weakness on regulated destructive actions with humanReviewRequired true, not ASI02 which is about missing allow-lists/scoping) and owasp-llm-top10-2025 LLM06 (excessive agency: 'require human approval for high-impact actions') - all three ids exist (SEBI catalog / registry structures for the catalog-less OWASP instruments) with regulator pairings matching the registry, so no correction is needed (unverifiable: the SARIF results array beyond the first 2000 characters - single-line export truncated by the reader and grep is blind to the gitignored kpis/data/raw tree - but the rule definition and every mapping input were confirmed).).","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S3"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.AA.S3"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-agentic-top10-2026","controlId":"ASI09"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-llm-top10-2025","controlId":"LLM06"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":"src/elicitation.ts","startLine":30,"endLine":44},"fingerprint":"f658ce80746ca24360bbbc6ea77d7913bf57efcbcb4882305d7036800cecb0f0","source":{"kind":"sarif","ruleId":"AGENT-ASI09-01","tool":"maxwell-agent-graph-auditor","toolVersion":"1.0.0"},"status":"triaged","slaDueAt":"2026-09-22T15:14:31Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.MA.S3","topic":"patch-sla","severity":"high","days":7},"relatedObservationIds":["obs_01M2K7B0MD6QPQYB5WX88W6X26"],"firstSeenAt":"2026-09-15T15:14:31Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-15T15:14:31Z","evidence":[{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/opencode/run_01M2GDZ3Q3S5WYCB3MV02QJXZ1.probe-agent-graph.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","sha256":"c3c7b9dc736d1407d3a96f196cc75bf759aeb1756332fa0e4691fca51f59a10e","description":"result 0 (AGENT-ASI09-01)"}],"tags":["agentic","static-probe","owasp-agentic-top10-2026:asi09","human-in-the-loop","mcp"],"provenance":{"harness":"opencode","generatedAt":"2026-09-15T23:48:58Z","sessionId":"453ecc6e-1346-418f-a2c0-1bfcead851c3","runId":"run_01M2GDZ3Q3S5WYCB3MV02QJXZ1","workflow":"impl-change-management","agent":"soc-ledger-keeper"},"supersedes":"fnd_01M2K7B0MJ68AR00YTNE2N00V2","initiativeId":"init_01M2KRVFNGEJFKP3NR1V9M2PM5"}
+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2K7B0MJQMT1S973WHW7K9GA","recordedAt":"2026-09-15T23:48:58Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"Write tools enabled by default: 11 of 19 write-capable tools have no approval and no allow-list","description":"src/common/config/userConfig.ts:96-103 `readOnly ... .default(false)`, :74-78 `disabledTools ... .default([])`, :79-94 confirmationRequiredTools defaulting to only 8 names (atlas-create-access-list, atlas-create-db-user, drop-database, drop-collection, delete-many, drop-index, atlas-streams-manage, atlas-streams-teardown). Unconfirmed write tools include update-many (bulk modify with upsert), insert-many, rename-collection, create-collection, create-index, atlas-upgrade-cluster, atlas-create-free-cluster, atlas-create-project, atlas-streams-build and the atlas-local create and delete deployment tools. The shipped deploy config (deploy/aws/Dockerfile:13) disables only the atlas-local category, so a model can bulk-modify pii and financial client records in qa and prod. Per-tool parameter validation is present (Zod argsShape on every tool), so the gap is the absent least-privilege default, not input validation; aiCodingPolicy.promptInjectionControls names tool-allowlist and human-approval-for-writes but the deployed configuration implements neither for this gateway. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S3. SLA topic: patch-sla. Refutation: evidence lens not refuted (Every substantive claim verified from files I opened: src/common/config/userConfig.ts:74-103 literally shows disabledTools .default([]) at 74-78, confirmationRequiredTools defaulting to exactly the 8 named tools at 79-94, and readOnly .default(false) at 95-103; the repo has 19 write-capable tools (9 mongodb, 8 atlas, 2 atlas-local; operationType spot-checked on update-many \"update\" and atlas-streams-build \"create\", Zod argsShape present) of which exactly the 11 the description lists name-for-name are unconfirmed; deploy/aws/Dockerfile:13 overrides only MDB_MCP_DISABLED_TOOLS=atlas-local (the root Dockerfile sets no tool limits, the azure bicep MDB_MCP_READ_ONLY:'true' template is not the AWS path the env records deploy, and the repo contains no settings.json/permission-map scoping that would exempt the rule); qa (internal) and prod (partner) both deploy this repo's deploy path with pii+financial data and aiCodingPolicy.promptInjectionControls matches sdlc/policy.json; the SARIF export exists at the cited path as the maxwell-agent-graph-auditor 1.0.0 log and contains a result with \"ruleId\":\"AGENT-ASI02-01\" whose own object carries a userConfig location with startLine 74 and endLine 103, a message discussing confirmationRequiredTools, and the workflow-computed fingerprint 5e8d5ad607ba7b8c4f85364640afdeca826d84ab45d32b497c7dba48e91dfb3d, its sha256 matching the digest attested in the auditor's own session transcript; severity high equals the sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S3 catalog defaultSeverity (catalog line 2249) and the evidence supports it, so no lower severity is warranted.); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (All five cited instruments apply (SEBI CSCRF binds the mid-size-re stock broker/DP and is first, DPDP Rules 2025 covers stock-brokers and is second, the OWASP/CSA frameworks are cross-sector and prescribed for LLM-agent companies by the skill's selection table), every controlId exists and its text covers the gap (PR.AA.S3 least privilege, DPDP 6(1)(b) access control with the tools-reach-personal-data condition met, ASI02 tool-misuse matching the asi02 tag and the over-broad-tool-side-effects weakness, LLM06 excessive agency, CSA 8.3 allowlist/human-confirmation practices named in the finding), and severity high is correctly derived per maxwell-conventions section 4 since the SARIF export carries no security-severity and the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S3 is high, with the gap confirmed in userConfig.ts:74-103 and deploy/aws/Dockerfile:13.).","severity":"