+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2KBJW4AHE221KPTRV1G60YC","recordedAt":"2026-09-15T23:48:58Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"mcp-gateway/mongodb-mcp-server: Human-confirmation gate for destructive MCP tools fails open for clients without elicitation support","description":"ASVS 5.0 L2 scope with agent-code lenses (LLM06, ASI02). destructive tools (drop-database, drop-collection, delete-many, drop-index, atlas-create-db-user, atlas-create-access-list, atlas-streams-manage, atlas-streams-teardown) are listed in confirmationRequiredTools by default (src/common/config/userConfig.ts:79-94) and ToolBase.invoke asks Elicitation.requestConfirmation before executing them (src/tools/tool.ts:491-513, 609-615); requestConfirmation returns true immediately when the MCP client does not declare the elicitation capability (src/elicitation.ts:30-33), so any client that omits that capability executes destructive operations against the pii/financial stores with no human approval. ExampleCo sdlc policy lists human-approval-for-writes as its prompt-injection control, and this is the code path meant to enforce it. Severity high from the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S3 (least privilege and segregation of duties); no CVSS computed because the caller already reaches the API - the defect removes a required human control rather than crossing a privilege boundary. SARIF result index 1.\n\nData flow: tools/call on MCP HTTP transport -> ToolBase.invoke requiresConfirmation (tool.ts:491-513) -> verifyConfirmed -> Elicitation.requestConfirmation returns true when supportsElicitation() is false (elicitation.ts:31-33) -> destructive tool executes against MongoDB\n\nExploit scenario: An MCP client (for example a compromised or prompt-injected agent runtime) sends initialize without the elicitation capability, then calls tools/call drop-database; the server skips the confirmation entirely and drops the database with no human ever seeing a prompt.\n\nImpact: On the partner-exposed prod gateway every confirmation-required destructive operation is effectively unattended for clients that omit one capability flag, defeating the human-approval-for-writes control of the company AI coding policy for a system holding pii and financial data; a prompt-injected agent (LLM06/ASI02) can destroy or rewrite client data before a human notices. Catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S3 is high; recorded as context, not as an uplift.\n\nRemediation: Fail closed: in Elicitation.requestConfirmation, return false (refuse the call) when the client does not support elicitation while a confirmation-required tool is invoked; optionally add a config flag to make confirmations mandatory for destructive tools regardless of client capability, and log every confirmation request and outcome as a security event.\n\nSource: maxwell-secure-code-reviewer agent analysis (execute-scr) at pinned commit aaa72a040db4c32f3d6488d5e28e2892a68e9ee0; no scanner SARIF log exists for this target.","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S3"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.AA.S3"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-llm-top10-2025","controlId":"LLM06"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-agentic-top10-2026","controlId":"ASI02"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":"src/elicitation.ts","startLine":30,"endLine":33},"fingerprint":"8ecab0bd0359448e815853d574c6ee79b09f539cdae6e54c38985a94f97274fe","source":{"kind":"agent-analysis","ruleId":"asvs-v2-confirmation-fail-open","tool":"secure-code-reviewer"},"status":"triaged","slaDueAt":"2026-09-22T19:42:44Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.MA.S3","topic":"patch-sla","severity":"high","days":7},"relatedObservationIds":["obs_01M2KBJW49PYVZW02VTCZBQA9F"],"firstSeenAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-15T19:42:44Z","eviden